# NEVER commit a database snapshot.
#
# These are dumps of the live system. They carry real customer names and
# real mobile numbers, and this repository is public — a snapshot pushed
# by accident is a data breach that cannot be taken back, because the
# object stays reachable in git history after the file is deleted.
#
# Keep the directory (so the tools have somewhere to write) and ignore
# everything in it.
*
!.gitignore
